ic countries join ankara  blames them for sheltering kurdish  activists that turkey considers enemies  of the state  there should be absolute security  guarantees here this is not just about  two candidate countries but also about  allied states who need to stop  supporting terrorist organizations  but officials said they were certain  those differences could be resolved  quickly meanwhile nothing will change  right away the finnish parliament must  ratify the decision and the nato  application process could take up to a  year  and we can cross straight to brussels  now and speak to our correspondent there  christine mundo hi christine can you  walk us through what still needs to  happen before finland and sweden  officially apply to join nato  good morning anya so effectively nato  membership needs the unanimous approval  of all of the alliances 30 members and  what that means  is that every single member state has to  go to their parliament and have that  ratified and this is why this process  could take up two months for his part  the nato secretary general said both  sweden and finland would be welcomed  with open arms that the accession  process would be quick but in reality it  does look like it would take at least a  few months  before all those processes those former  processes can conclude in each member's  parliament  so it's going to take a while if  everyone agrees but how likely is it  that turkey could veto finland and  sweden's membership bid  well turkey's opposition does pose a  serious threat and as we've just heard  in the report there there does seem to  be confidence among the young other  members states um and and allies for  example the secretary general said he  was confident that they would find  common ground and reach consensus over  the matter but of course because nato  membership requires the unanimous  approval of every single member state if  turkey doesn't come to the table  that could effectively put a stop to  this process  now if 